-academy-id "q-12282" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014125/assets/fa0dbfe03050a0ca52f2fbe1988a9e6475cd24437c619dba27a4fed984736fc1.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 6=9.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=3\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,8\\,|\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =72.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-12282/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-12282"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-12283/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "bffad3b6-b172-5d32-bfab-fc60a5402105" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12283/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "42b6224f-923a-5360-a485-4326f1f0214f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12283/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "917403b5-2e39-5636-948d-cea29a8dd856" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12283/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "a020910f-f65d-528c-9350-402b2832f3fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12283/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "ebd3e3a4-9052-5ad8-bb54-92512b963762" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12283/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c3f5854-8cda-5f26-85ca-7ed82bad6878" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-12283/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-12283/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" "q-12283/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-12283/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-12283/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-12283/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-12283" :question/id #uuid "9e63b622-9c7c-55b8-a345-80a493030152" :question/math-academy-id "q-12283" :question/problem "The unit square $D$ has vertices $(1,0),(0,0),(0,1),(1,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014125/assets/3cbf4ce4422e043cedb73e9b10bba11e9cb1e64352ff182eff8aaa0046c4e8f3.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=1\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=4\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 2=10.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,10\\,|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-12283/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-12283"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316583/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "077156d1-acb4-53e2-84ba-b9c83513c24b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316583/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6af86557-150d-5700-b396-1be945e8d24d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316583/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer-field/choices ["q-316583/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316583" :question/id #uuid "8790e788-5572-5ddf-b551-3d829cda7a34" :question/math-academy-id "q-316583" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014125/assets/2318282d0f822fdec18bee5808a3d6be2d477cb106f124c32d4f0d589dac0978.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 2=3.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 1=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,5\\,|\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316583/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316583"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316593/field-1/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "9fa64d19-2d9f-5d52-ba81-ecb3b8246af9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316593/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "83c2a10c-2b59-5da3-b7d5-01e7b17e3f53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316593/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d7b9dfc4-e0e8-520f-a98c-6f020a31ae43" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316593/field-1/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer-field/choices ["q-316593/field-1/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" "q-316593/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316593" :question/id #uuid "968e73f9-2aca-5739-8110-8553403d16ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-316593" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014125/assets/9eb3ccd040b0a8bca45f30780e62bd77fdd3333005e748ad40d47afc20f82ea4.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,(3+3)\\cdot 2=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=0\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 3=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-6\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316593/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316593"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316598/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "81001409-c569-533a-a2b7-efcf7f397e46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316598/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f259a8c8-cae9-5672-86ca-ce9c8aca1649" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316598/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer-field/choices ["q-316598/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316598" :question/id #uuid "75fce5ef-ce16-54b6-beee-1ddbfa19c810" :question/math-academy-id "q-316598" :question/problem "The unit square $D$ has vertices $(1,0),(0,0),(0,1),(1,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014125/assets/6805467a24cb40559f205cbfcecc4f5a34ff2ec6ebda8ae67f997c02f123b53c.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=1\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-4)\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 1=-12-2=-14.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-14\\,|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-316598/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316598"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
